{"author":"RebarBotNava","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","author_sig":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","data":{"body":"REMEDIATION VERIFIED (read-only git evidence, 2026-08-04 ~15:40 UTC) — the incident itself is fully remediated; two ACs remain that this ticket's text does not let me tick.\n\n## What was verified, and how\n\n**AC2 — offending comment removed from `tickets` history and the branch pushing again: SATISFIED.**\n\n1. The leaking commit object is gone from the local object store:\n   `git cat-file -e 0a09e51c9fbcb27a2beea21fea12c23c5ac89f38` -> exit 1 (\"not our ref\"). The object does not exist locally at all (not merely unreachable).\n2. The credential-bearing event file is absent from the `tickets` branch tip AND its entire history:\n   `git log --oneline tickets -- '129e-2d88-cce2-492c/1785809605060290001-7a5384a0-53eb-4de8-a5fc-06519ffa6b5c-COMMENT.json'` -> 0 lines;\n   `git cat-file -e tickets:<that path>` -> fatal, path does not exist. The other 5 COMMENT events under 129e remain intact (surgical removal).\n3. Pushes flow: from `.tickets-tracker`, `git fetch origin tickets && git merge-base --is-ancestor tickets origin/tickets` -> exit 0, with `rev-list --count` 0 ahead / 0 behind — local `tickets` and `origin/tickets` are identical. The store's auto-push (including the writes for this very verification: the claim of this ticket and this comment) is reaching origin normally.\n4. Provenance of the fix: an operator-directed session on 2026-08-04 ~05:02–05:40 UTC ran `git filter-branch --index-filter --prune-empty` over the affected range (dropping exactly that one file; commit count 62973 -> 62972; tree diff vs old tip = that single file deletion), merged with `origin/tickets`, pushed, then deleted all backups (`tickets-backup-remove-0a09e51c`, `refs/original/refs/heads/tickets`, and the pre-existing `tickets-backup-secretleak`), expired reflogs, and ran `git gc --prune=now`. Evidence in (1) confirms the purge held.\n\n**AC4 — a decision recorded on whether ticket event payloads are scanned on write: SATISFIED (decision = YES, scan on write; recorded in e7a9-35fa-1d58-4095).**\nTicket e7a9-35fa-1d58-4095 (\"Store accepts secret-bearing event bodies\") records the decision and the plan: a deterministic secret screen at the event-append seam (the single choke point all writers share), rejecting/redacting high-confidence credential patterns BEFORE the event file is written, with regression fixtures so placeholder forms don't fire. e4f4-295b-2c03-44c4 records the incident-class analysis (shell command-substitution in double-quoted comment bodies) and the refuse-don't-redact rationale. The decision this AC asked for exists and is durable; the IMPLEMENTATION lives in e7a9 (still open).\n\n## What I could NOT verify, and why the boxes stay unticked\n\n**AC1 — both credentials rotated: NOT VERIFIABLE from this checkout.** No ticket, comment, or session record states the Anthropic key and GitHub PAT were rotated. This is an operator fact; a prior session's comment on this ticket reached the same conclusion. The AC text demands the rotation itself, so it cannot be ticked by deferral.\n\n**AC3 — a rejected auto-push surfaces to the writing agent instead of failing silently: NOT YET TRUE.** This is exactly e7a9's third AC (\"Store push failures log the git rejection reason (GH013 line + offending path) instead of a bare retry count\"), and e7a9 is open/unimplemented. The AC text here demands the behavior, not a tracking ticket, so it cannot honestly be ticked by deferral either.\n\n## Disposition\n\nThe INCIDENT (blocked pushes, credential-bearing history) is fully remediated and evidenced above. The ticket cannot honestly close while AC1 (operator rotation attestation) and AC3 (push-failure surfacing, owned by e7a9) remain unsatisfied. Ticking AC2 + AC4 and leaving the ticket for: (a) an operator to attest rotation on AC1, and (b) e7a9's landing to satisfy AC3."},"env_id":"ade0f2ef-51cc-45a2-bb97-c09846cd3df5","event_type":"COMMENT","timestamp":1785858365408749001,"uuid":"d5193909-d7f3-4578-bd28-2851051db4f6"}